Note: End-to-end test of the @test framework surface (Phase 35 / TEST-01).
Note:
Note: Phase 46 (D-07): ported from the removed pure-Flow legacy assertion library
Note: (assertTrue/assertEqual/runTest/summary) to the canonical @test module.
Note: The legacy asserts RETURNED Bool and printed PASS/FAIL — the @test asserts
Note: THROW AssertionException on failure, so every original FAIL case is ported
Note: as a POSITIVE assertion of the negation via the registered `not` builtin.
Note:
Note: Run via `dotnet run --project flow-cli -- test tests/test_test_library.flow`
Note: to actually EXECUTE the bodies. The legacy `flow-interpreter` path only
Note: REGISTERS the tests and emits the "ALL TESTS REGISTERED" sentinel.

use "@std"
use "@test"

Note: ===== assert (Bool) =====
(test "assert true does not throw" lazy((assert true)))
(test "assert FAIL case inverted" lazy((assert (not false))))

Note: assertFalse PASS/FAIL ported to (assert (not ...))
(test "assertFalse PASS case" lazy((assert (not false))))
(test "assertFalse FAIL case inverted" lazy((assert (not (not true)))))

Note: ===== assertEq (equality) =====
(test "assertEq Int PASS case" lazy((assertEq 2 2)))
(test "assertEq Int FAIL case inverted" lazy((assert (not (equals 2 3)))))
(test "assertEq String PASS case" lazy((assertEq "hi" "hi")))

Note: assertNotEqual ported to (assert (not (equals ...)))
(test "assertNotEqual PASS case" lazy((assert (not (equals 2 3)))))
(test "assertNotEqual FAIL case inverted" lazy((assert (not (not (equals 2 2))))))

Note: ===== ordering comparisons =====
(test "assertLess PASS case" lazy((assert (lt 1 2))))
(test "assertLess FAIL case inverted" lazy((assert (not (lt 2 1)))))
(test "assertGreater PASS case" lazy((assert (gt 5 3))))
(test "assertGreater FAIL case inverted" lazy((assert (not (gt 3 5)))))
(test "assertLessOrEqual PASS equal" lazy((assert (lte 2 2))))
(test "assertLessOrEqual FAIL case inverted" lazy((assert (not (lte 3 2)))))
(test "assertGreaterOrEqual PASS equal" lazy((assert (gte 2 2))))
(test "assertGreaterOrEqual FAIL case inverted" lazy((assert (not (gte 1 2)))))

Note: ===== approximate equality =====
Note: |1.0 - 1.0001| <= 0.001 is true (PASS); |1.0 - 1.5| <= 0.001 is false,
Note: ported as the positive assertion that the diff is GREATER than epsilon.
(test "assertApprox PASS within epsilon" lazy((assert (lte (abs (sub 1.0 1.0001)) 0.001))))
(test "assertApprox FAIL outside epsilon inverted" lazy((assert (gt (abs (sub 1.0 1.5)) 0.001))))

Note: ===== inline test (was runTest) =====
(test "inline test: 2 + 2 = 4" lazy((assertEq (add 2 2) 4)))

(print "ALL TESTS REGISTERED")
